# Lab: Configure Identity Providers

**Exam Domain:** 1 — Implement identities in Microsoft Entra ID
**Topic:** External identities — SAML/WS-Fed IdP federation, Google federation, Facebook federation
**Platform:** Microsoft Entra admin center + Azure portal
**Status:** ✅ Complete

---

## 🎯 Lab Objectives

This lab covers three identity provider configurations:

1. **SAML/WS-Fed IdP Federation** — federate with a partner organisation's identity provider
2. **Google Federation** — allow Gmail users to sign in as B2B guests
3. **Facebook Federation** — allow Facebook users to sign in via self-service sign-up

---

## 🏢 Scenario

Your organisation works with external partners, and you want to enable seamless sign-in for guest users without requiring them to create separate Microsoft Entra accounts. You will configure multiple external identity providers so that guests can use their own organisational or social identities to access shared resources.

---

## 📋 Prerequisites

| Requirement | Detail |
|---|---|
| Tenant | Microsoft Entra tenant |
| Role required | Global Administrator |
| Google setup | Google account + access to Google Developers Console |
| Facebook setup | Facebook account + access to Facebook Developers Console |
| Self-service sign-up | Must be enabled for Facebook federation |

