## ✅ Key Learning Outcomes

- Understand when SAML/WS-Fed IdP federation applies vs Google/Facebook
- Configure Google as an identity provider for B2B guest users
- Create a Google developer project and obtain client credentials
- Configure Facebook as an identity provider for self-service sign-up
- Create a Facebook app and obtain App ID and App Secret
- Understand the end-user sign-in experience for each IdP
- Know how to remove/delete federation configurations
- Understand the impact of deleting federation on existing guest users

---

## 🔑 Key Concepts for SC-300 Exam

| Concept | What to Know |
|---|---|
| SAML/WS-Fed federation | For organisations with their own IdP (e.g. AD FS, Okta, Ping) |
| Google federation | For Gmail users signing in as B2B guests |
| Facebook federation | Only for self-service sign-up — cannot be used for B2B invitations |
| Federation scope | Tied to domain namespaces (e.g. contoso.com) |
| Existing guest users | Federation change does NOT affect already-redeemed invitations |
| Redemption status reset | Required to change auth method for existing guest users |
| WebView deprecation | Google deprecated embedded WebView sign-in from September 2021 |
| Removing federation | Existing guests using that IdP will lose sign-in ability |
| B2B vs self-service | Google = B2B invitations; Facebook = self-service sign-up user flows only |
